NodOS is free to use, study, change and share. It may not be sold, and nobody
may make money from it. The rest of this text spells that out.

1. DEFINITIONS

"NodOS" means the software in this repository, in source or compiled form,
together with its documentation.

"You" means anyone using NodOS under this license.

"Derivative" means any work that is based on, copied from, or includes a
substantial part of NodOS, including modified versions, forks, ports and
anything that bundles NodOS.

"Commercial Use" means any use of NodOS or a Derivative that earns or is meant
to earn money or any other payment, benefit or advantage from NodOS itself.
Without limiting that, it includes:

  (a) selling, licensing or renting NodOS or a Derivative, or charging for a
      copy, download, update, key, activation or access;
  (b) offering NodOS or a Derivative as a paid or ad-supported service, hosted
      product, subscription, "premium" tier or feature gate;
  (c) charging for support, installation, setup, configuration, consulting,
      training, customization or maintenance of NodOS or a Derivative;
  (d) including NodOS or a Derivative in a product, device, image or service
      that is sold or is otherwise a source of revenue;
  (e) earning from advertising, sponsorship, affiliate links, paywalls or data
      collection placed on or around NodOS or a Derivative, or on a website,
      video or channel whose main purpose is to distribute or promote it;
  (f) charging for access to a Derivative's source code, builds or releases.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

Subject to the rest of this license, you may, free of charge:

  (a) use NodOS for any purpose that is not Commercial Use, including at home,
      at school, at work, and to manage the servers of a company or other
      organization you belong to. Running NodOS on your own infrastructure is
      not Commercial Use, even if that infrastructure supports a business,
      provided nobody pays for NodOS itself or for access to it;
  (b) download, read, copy and study the source code;
  (c) modify the source code and build your own versions;
  (d) share NodOS and your Derivatives with anyone, in source or compiled form,
      as long as you do so for free and follow section 3.

3. CONDITIONS

  (a) Free only. You may not charge for NodOS or any Derivative, and you may
      not make Commercial Use of either.
  (b) Keep this license. Every copy or Derivative you share must include this
      license text and the copyright notice, and must be shared under this same
      license. You may not add terms that restrict what this license allows or
      that allow what it forbids.
  (c) Say what you changed. A modified version must carry a clear notice that
      it was modified, by whom, and that it is not the official NodOS.
  (d) Source stays available. If you share a compiled Derivative, you must also
      make its complete source available, free of charge.
  (e) No passing off. You may not use the NodOS name or logo in a way that
      suggests your Derivative is the official release or is endorsed by the
      project. See docs/legal/trademarks.md.
  (f) No circumvention. You may not remove or disable the update signature
      check in order to distribute builds that pretend to be official ones.

